+## Scoped fix round 1: I1 and I2
+
+The [independent static review](task-11-forward-ddl-static-review-20261024.md) retained **two Important** findings on the original exact SQL. This R1 is the same author's proposed repair for later independent adjudication; it is not a static-review PASS or a MySQL execution result. The original SQL/report/manifest SHA pins are preserved in the R1 manifest.
+
+* **I1 — exact stored vocabulary.** MySQL's `ascii_bin` is a PAD SPACE collation for VARCHAR comparisons, so equality alone can admit trailing spaces. R1 pairs each allowed `local_state` literal with its exact UTF-8 octet length (9 or 12) and each `local_reason` literal with its own exact length (21, 25, or 26). The declared column types and complete UNDECIDED/NEVER_MARKED null tuple stay intact. This excludes a stored trailing-space variant of any accepted literal while retaining the same ASCII binary collation; an isolated negative-row probe remains required. [MySQL 8.4 CHAR/VARCHAR comparison rules](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/char.html).
+* **I2 — CHECK-used FK columns.** The [MySQL 8.4 CHECK restrictions](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/create-table-check-constraints.html) prohibit FK referential-action clauses on columns appearing in a CHECK. The two nullable decision FKs now omit explicit `ON UPDATE` and `ON DELETE`; all four other FKs still spell `RESTRICT`. The [MySQL 8.4 FK manual](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/create-table-foreign-keys.html) says an omitted action defaults to `NO ACTION`, and InnoDB applies `NO ACTION` immediately with the same restriction as `RESTRICT`. This is a documented semantic choice, not evidence that MySQL 8.4.6 accepted this exact combined CREATE. The later isolated CREATE/negative-row/FK preservation probe is mandatory before freeze/application. The full SQL decision tuple and all six FKs remain present.
 
